 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The one that, the one who",
     "texto": [
      "**Который** agrees with the noun it refers to in gender and number: **друг, который живёт**; **подруга, которая работает**; **окно, которое открыто**; **друзья, которые живут**. Its case depends on the function it has within the relative clause.",
      "In **книга, которую я читаю**, the relative is feminine singular because of **книга**, and it is in the accusative because it is the object of **читаю**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "In order to...",
     "texto": [
      "**Чтобы + infinitive** expresses purpose when the subject is the same: **Я иду в магазин, чтобы купить хлеб** («I am going to the shop to buy bread»).",
      "When you want another person to do something, use **чтобы + past form**: **Я хочу, чтобы ты пришёл** («I want you to come»). **Пришёл** has the past form, but here it expresses a future wish. **Хочу рассказать** («I want to tell») keeps the same subject and does not take **чтобы**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Gender, number and case of который",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Form of the relative",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Antecedent",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Function in the relative clause",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Example and translation",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
